# omni-deployer - secrets.env template (code-plan C9 never-commit guardrail)
#
# The deployer reads secrets from `secrets.env` (gitignored, generated
# locally - never committed). This template lists the well-known entries.
# Copy it to `secrets.env` and fill in REAL values; NEVER commit secrets.env
# or any file holding live secrets - the pre-commit hook and CI job
# (scripts/secret-scan.py) block them.
#
# All values below are placeholders (xxxx). Replace every xxxx before use.
# GITHUB_APP_KEY is the multiline PEM private key of the GitHub App used for
# git pushes (populated by the omniagent git plugin at runtime from the
# secrets store; keep the value out of every repo).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=xxxx
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=xxxx-your-deepseek-api-key
OPENCODE_API_KEY=xxxx-your-opencode-go-api-key
GITHUB_APP_ID=xxxx
GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=xxxx
# GITHUB_APP_KEY=xxxx (multiline PEM; paste only into local secrets.env)
#
# DEV STACK (omnidev) NOTE: `shared.setup()` seeds every entry of this file
# into the stack's own secrets store, so the dev stack authenticates its LLM
# providers with the keys defined HERE (model config: config/models.yml
# `api_key: $secret:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`). The dev `omni` profile pins the
# deepseek provider, so an omnidev stack set up WITHOUT this file has no
# provider key and every deepseek LLM call fails authentication. That used to
# surface as a bare upstream 401; it is now an explicit
# "Provider 'deepseek' has an unresolved API key reference
# $secret:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY" error, and `omnidev.py setup` reports the missing
# entry at the end of every setup run.

# --- external-plan X7: new credential classes (never commit) ---------------
# Values for these credential classes live ONLY in the secrets store or in an
# untracked .env file. Committing them is blocked by scripts/secret-scan.py and
# .gitleaks.toml (see the session-state / credentials guidance in .gitignore).
#   EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=<app password>     himalaya password / password.command value
#   MODEM_SIM_PIN=<SIM PIN>               SMS modem / SIM PIN
#   TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=<account SID>      Twilio account SID (AC...)
#   TWILIO_API_KEY=<API key SID>          Twilio API key SID (SK...)
#   TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=<auth token>        Twilio auth token
#   TOTP_SECRET=<base32 secret>           TOTP/HOTP shared secret
#   PLAYWRIGHT_STORAGE_STATE=<file path>  per-site session file - never committed
